<title>FRANCE: Pinault-Printemps up ahead of results.</title>
<headline>Pinault-Printemps up ahead of results.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Pinault-Printemps-Redoute were up sharply on Wednesday ahead of the retail group's announcement of its 1996 results.</p>
<p>The stock was up 3.65 percent at 2,329 francs at 1025 GMT, while the bourse was 0.7 percent higher.</p>
<p>&quot;It had fallen a lot recently and was oversold,&quot; said a broker who expects a 1996 profit close to two billion francs, up from 1.52 billion for 1995. Another brokerage estimated a profit of 1.93 billion francs in its daily stock comment.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
